    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s only historic building is an early‑1900s school that was abandoned when newer facilities opened in Socorro.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dryheatblog.com/exploring-the-town-of-escondida-new-mexico/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The abandoned school sits amid a thicket of mesquite, a thorny shrub that can tear through clothing if you brush against it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dryheatblog.com/exploring-the-town-of-escondida-new-mexico/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "While searching for the school, a visitor discovered an abandoned house, revealing Escondida’s quiet, forgotten architecture.",
